WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.617 --> 00:00:04.321
- Our mind is the control
tower of our life.

00:00:04.321 --> 00:00:07.287
Whatever happens in our
life starts right here.

00:00:07.287 --> 00:00:09.876
And I don't think you should
ever live to the point

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.975
you think, well, I've reached it now.

00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:13.200
Then what do you do?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.159
You just die.

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:17.725
People don't realize
that money is dangerous.

00:00:17.725 --> 00:00:21.236
Somebody says, well what could
be dangerous about money?

00:00:21.236 --> 00:00:22.824
It's what it does.

00:00:22.824 --> 00:00:25.045
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:25.045 --> 00:00:27.840
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.989
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:32.847
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:35.092
we're going to learn from
Pastor Charles Stanley

00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:37.673
and my take on his Top
10 Rules of Success.

00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:39.940
Rule number three is my personal favorite

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.737
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:44.468
And, as always, as you're listening,

00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:46.281
if something really resonates with you,

00:00:46.281 --> 00:00:48.288
if there's a message that
really holds true to you,

00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:50.190
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.839
and put it in quotes so that
other people can be inspired.

00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:54.499
And when you write it down it's much

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:57.059
more likely to stick
with yourself as well.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:00:58.177
Enjoy.

00:00:58.177 --> 00:01:00.712
(swooshing and boom)

00:01:00.712 --> 00:01:04.462
(upbeat inspirational music)

00:01:11.001 --> 00:01:13.937
- A person who's willing
to just take it easy,

00:01:13.937 --> 00:01:16.104
do whatever comes natural,

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:19.198
don't have any real goals in life,

00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:21.660
don't strive for anything,
and I think part of

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.152
the reason for that is
that people are lazy.

00:01:24.152 --> 00:01:25.874
They want the easy way out.

00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:27.484
They don't believe that they

00:01:27.484 --> 00:01:29.107
can accomplish anything in life.

00:01:29.107 --> 00:01:32.182
They don't have a sense of
purpose, they have no goals.

00:01:32.182 --> 00:01:34.734
They don't know how to
set goals in their life.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.757
And what they do is,
they waste a great deal

00:01:37.757 --> 00:01:40.589
of their life because they
have no sense of direction

00:01:40.589 --> 00:01:43.304
and they just settle for
whatever comes their way.

00:01:43.304 --> 00:01:45.764
And, oftentimes, thinking
that they can't do any better

00:01:45.764 --> 00:01:47.929
and looking around at what
other people are doing

00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:50.142
and thinking well, I'm
as good as they are.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:53.483
And they miss life, settling
for less than the best.

00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:55.692
- Why do you think so many people do that?

00:01:55.692 --> 00:01:58.978
Why are they so willing to
settle for less than God's best?

00:01:58.978 --> 00:02:01.569
- Well I think they don't really believe

00:02:01.569 --> 00:02:03.861
that they can achieve and accomplish.

00:02:03.861 --> 00:02:06.562
They look around and see
what other people are doing

00:02:06.562 --> 00:02:08.594
and they think, well, I'm
as well off as they are,

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:09.546
but that's not the issue.

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:11.537
The issue is, what is the
will of God for my life?

00:02:11.537 --> 00:02:12.721
What could I accomplish?

00:02:12.721 --> 00:02:14.506
What could I achieve if I really

00:02:14.506 --> 00:02:16.647
and truly set my mind to do it?

00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:20.291
And I think sometimes
it's just pure laziness

00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:22.975
that people don't have
a sense of direction.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.720
But, they don't want to do anything else

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:29.011
and it's a tragedy that a
person can live out their life

00:02:29.011 --> 00:02:31.936
with gifts and skills and
abilities and talents that God's

00:02:31.936 --> 00:02:35.772
given them and just settle for
doing whatever comes natural.

00:02:35.772 --> 00:02:37.844
- What are some of the warning signs

00:02:37.844 --> 00:02:39.879
that we are living a 'settled for' life?

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:42.828
- I think number one
there's no progress in life.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.055
Not making any progress financially,

00:02:45.055 --> 00:02:47.917
in relationships, in your
relationship to the Lord.

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.384
Things are just still the status quo.

00:02:50.384 --> 00:02:52.729
And you're sort of
running around in circles

00:02:52.729 --> 00:02:56.324
and spending time and living
from one weekend to the other.

00:02:56.324 --> 00:02:58.897
And I think people who
do that, they've settled

00:02:58.897 --> 00:03:01.918
for far less than God
has intended for them.

00:03:01.918 --> 00:03:04.521
Well, God wants us all to be courageous

00:03:04.521 --> 00:03:08.112
because he knows we'll face
times in life and situations

00:03:08.112 --> 00:03:10.823
and circumstances that it takes more than

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.656
just the desire, it takes courage.

00:03:14.544 --> 00:03:17.246
Many people operate on the basis of fear,

00:03:17.246 --> 00:03:19.491
on the basis of what other people think.

00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:22.912
We as believers should operate
on the basis of courage.

00:03:22.912 --> 00:03:25.609
Courage to say no when we ought to say no.

00:03:25.609 --> 00:03:29.494
Courage to say yes when we should say yes.

00:03:29.494 --> 00:03:31.712
So what kind of courage do you have?

00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:33.736
Is yours sort of floating between

00:03:33.736 --> 00:03:35.900
depending on the situation?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.072
Or do you know the difference between

00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:40.472
right and wrong for your life?

00:03:40.472 --> 00:03:42.643
And you've made up your mind.

00:03:42.643 --> 00:03:46.396
Our mind is the control tower of our life.

00:03:46.396 --> 00:03:49.410
Whatever happens in our
life starts right here.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.490
All of our decisions are there.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:54.311
And the truth is, whatever
we are today is the result

00:03:54.311 --> 00:03:57.521
of what we've been thinking
about all those years.

00:03:57.521 --> 00:04:01.625
The Bible says, as a man
thinketh in his heart, so is he.

00:04:01.625 --> 00:04:04.046
So if you don't like
what's going on around you

00:04:04.046 --> 00:04:06.262
maybe you should ask
yourself the question,

00:04:06.262 --> 00:04:08.163
"What am I thinking about?"

00:04:08.163 --> 00:04:09.886
What do I think about myself,

00:04:09.886 --> 00:04:11.869
what do I think about other people?

00:04:11.869 --> 00:04:15.798
Because what we think about
is really what controls us.

00:04:15.798 --> 00:04:19.085
For example, our relationship to God,

00:04:19.085 --> 00:04:21.099
our relationship to each other,

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:23.198
our sense of direction in life,

00:04:23.198 --> 00:04:25.981
whatever we accomplish,
our failures in life.

00:04:25.981 --> 00:04:29.423
All of that is a result
of the way we think.

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:31.844
And oftentimes we forget that,

00:04:31.844 --> 00:04:34.118
that this is the control tower.

00:04:34.118 --> 00:04:37.951
That everything else is
a result of how we think.

00:04:37.951 --> 00:04:40.128
And we can't control everybody else

00:04:40.128 --> 00:04:42.374
and control all of our circumstances,

00:04:42.374 --> 00:04:44.950
but we are going to
respond to circumstances

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.502
in one way or the other.

00:04:46.502 --> 00:04:50.350
And so, when I think
about how this affects us,

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.739
I think about the fact
that many people are

00:04:52.739 --> 00:04:55.998
where they are because of wrong thinking.

00:04:55.998 --> 00:04:58.222
And so they don't like where they are.

00:04:58.222 --> 00:05:01.213
Other folks are where they
are because of right thinking,

00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:03.494
because they've been
thinking the right way.

00:05:03.494 --> 00:05:04.998
What you have to ask is this,

00:05:04.998 --> 00:05:07.598
what is it that determines what I think?

00:05:07.598 --> 00:05:11.499
This mind of yours controls
everything else in your life.

00:05:11.499 --> 00:05:14.375
You say, well what about all
the other parts of my life?

00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:17.432
We respond to the way we think.

00:05:17.432 --> 00:05:20.363
And so if we think right we're
going to have one response.

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:22.709
We think wrongly, we're
going to have another.

00:05:22.709 --> 00:05:26.417
Very important that we
understand how that works.

00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:28.566
So this requires me to understand

00:05:28.566 --> 00:05:30.621
how to control my thoughts.

00:05:30.621 --> 00:05:33.461
If I want to think right,
if I want to think Godly,

00:05:33.461 --> 00:05:36.412
if I want to think holy, if
I want to think righteously,

00:05:36.412 --> 00:05:38.622
right here is where it starts.

00:05:38.622 --> 00:05:41.522
And many people lose it right here.

00:05:41.522 --> 00:05:44.572
They don't think right,
they don't think Godly.

00:05:44.572 --> 00:05:46.941
They don't think like
they're worth anything.

00:05:46.941 --> 00:05:49.204
And they say, well, you
know I just never had

00:05:49.204 --> 00:05:51.526
the opportunity or I
just never will be that,

00:05:51.526 --> 00:05:53.932
or I'm just this and I'm not that.

00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:56.429
This is why people who are very beautiful

00:05:56.429 --> 00:05:58.461
can think they're ugly.

00:05:58.461 --> 00:06:02.643
And people who are very
skinny can think they're fat.

00:06:02.643 --> 00:06:05.543
And they refuse to eat because they think,

00:06:05.543 --> 00:06:09.061
they look in the mirror and
they don't see what's reality.

00:06:09.061 --> 00:06:12.349
And so your mind controls
every aspect of your life.

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:15.744
In fact, what you think
determines how you live.

00:06:15.744 --> 00:06:18.733
What you think determines
how your relationship to God,

00:06:18.733 --> 00:06:20.694
as we said, your relationship to others,

00:06:20.694 --> 00:06:22.711
your relationship to yourself.

00:06:22.711 --> 00:06:25.839
And many people start out in life defeated

00:06:25.839 --> 00:06:28.637
because of the influence of their parents,

00:06:28.637 --> 00:06:30.533
their grandparents, that tell them

00:06:30.533 --> 00:06:33.293
they'll never amount to anything.

00:06:33.293 --> 00:06:36.101
Or this is wrong with them,
or that's wrong with them.

00:06:36.101 --> 00:06:40.497
And as a result, they go
through life what, having heard,

00:06:40.497 --> 00:06:45.144
written in their minds,
impressed in their thinking,

00:06:45.144 --> 00:06:47.263
if my mama said it, my daddy said it

00:06:47.263 --> 00:06:50.742
and my grandmother said it,
it must be true, therefore.

00:06:50.742 --> 00:06:54.573
And oftentimes, people
are ruined as a result of

00:06:54.573 --> 00:06:58.283
what they have been taught
or what they've heard

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:00.601
from someone that they value very highly.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:03.767
That our love and desire for
material things can cause us

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:07.097
to miss the most important thing in life.

00:07:07.097 --> 00:07:11.314
People don't realize
that money is dangerous.

00:07:11.314 --> 00:07:14.889
Somebody says, well what could
be dangerous about money?

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:16.752
It's what it does.

00:07:16.752 --> 00:07:20.753
It's the attitude people have,
that if I have enough money

00:07:20.753 --> 00:07:24.032
I can go where I want to
go, do what I want to do,

00:07:24.032 --> 00:07:27.034
marry who I want to marry,
wear what I want to wear,

00:07:27.034 --> 00:07:29.866
drive what I want to drive,
live where I want to live,

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:33.428
eat whatever I want to eat
and on and on and on it goes.

00:07:33.428 --> 00:07:36.371
That may be some of
things that money can do,

00:07:36.371 --> 00:07:38.518
but that doesn't satisfy you.

00:07:38.518 --> 00:07:41.178
But think about this, you
can have all the money

00:07:41.178 --> 00:07:44.837
in the world you want if
you don't have good health,

00:07:44.837 --> 00:07:46.669
you can't buy it.

00:07:46.669 --> 00:07:48.964
If you're not, listen, if you don't have

00:07:48.964 --> 00:07:51.316
anybody to love, you can't buy it.

00:07:51.316 --> 00:07:54.793
If you don't have anyone who
loves you, you can't buy it.

00:07:54.793 --> 00:07:58.960
In other words, you can't
buy peace, joy, happiness,

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:03.864
contentment and you certainly
cannot buy eternal life.

00:08:03.864 --> 00:08:06.477
Money can do some things, it can do

00:08:06.477 --> 00:08:08.549
many good things in the right hands.

00:08:08.549 --> 00:08:12.525
But it can't satisfy the
longing of your soul.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:15.751
It can't satisfy the
longing of your heart.

00:08:15.751 --> 00:08:18.417
And when I think about the
future and I think about all

00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:21.842
the possibilities and living
in this age of electronics.

00:08:21.842 --> 00:08:24.033
I mean, we can learn so much and all of

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.213
the information's right at our fingertips,

00:08:26.213 --> 00:08:27.762
and the opportunities we have.

00:08:27.762 --> 00:08:30.459
I would hate to think I'd
reached my full potential, no.

00:08:30.459 --> 00:08:33.396
And I don't think you should
ever live to the point

00:08:33.396 --> 00:08:35.721
you think well, I've reached it now.

00:08:35.721 --> 00:08:36.996
Then what do you do?

00:08:36.996 --> 00:08:39.985
You just die and I think
many people die early

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:43.322
because they limit what
their potential is.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.489
Keep learning.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.404
When you cease to learn,
you cease to grow.

00:08:48.404 --> 00:08:49.931
When you cease to learn,

00:08:49.931 --> 00:08:52.554
you sort of begin to decay a little bit.

00:08:52.554 --> 00:08:56.685
You are to learn to how to stay healthy.

00:08:56.685 --> 00:08:58.629
And you say well, how do I do that?

00:08:58.629 --> 00:09:01.809
Well, the proper diet
and exercise and rest,

00:09:01.809 --> 00:09:03.023
that's part of it.

00:09:03.023 --> 00:09:06.761
In other words, we're
not healthy by accident.

00:09:06.761 --> 00:09:09.266
It's by learning some key things in life

00:09:09.266 --> 00:09:11.109
that really make a difference.

00:09:11.109 --> 00:09:15.361
And when we keep learning
something happens in our life.

00:09:15.361 --> 00:09:17.665
For example, you and
I are living in an age

00:09:17.665 --> 00:09:19.970
when we've had to keep learning.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.061
Because when I was born there were

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:26.106
no computers that I
knew of, in 1900 and 32.

00:09:26.106 --> 00:09:29.571
So, we go back and you look at your life

00:09:29.571 --> 00:09:33.379
and think about all the things
that you've had to learn

00:09:33.379 --> 00:09:37.547
that your predecessors and
your parents didn't have

00:09:37.547 --> 00:09:40.292
to learn because they didn't even exist.

00:09:40.292 --> 00:09:43.268
So if you're going to be useful
all the days of your life

00:09:43.268 --> 00:09:46.179
you've got to be willing to keep learning.

00:09:46.179 --> 00:09:50.909
So I would simply say that a
lazy brain is an aging brain.

00:09:50.909 --> 00:09:53.085
You don't want to learn, what happens?

00:09:53.085 --> 00:09:54.533
You start decaying.

00:09:54.533 --> 00:09:58.594
And so, there's something
interesting and exciting

00:09:58.594 --> 00:10:02.015
about learning things in
life no matter who you are

00:10:02.015 --> 00:10:04.474
and no matter what your age might be.

00:10:04.474 --> 00:10:08.641
Rejection is probably the most
painful of all the emotions.

00:10:11.669 --> 00:10:14.063
And the truth is, all of
us have been rejected,

00:10:14.063 --> 00:10:15.819
either by somebody or some group

00:10:15.819 --> 00:10:18.246
or something at some point in life.

00:10:18.246 --> 00:10:22.118
And so the question is,
how did you respond?

00:10:22.118 --> 00:10:23.725
And if I should ask you well,

00:10:23.725 --> 00:10:25.410
did that rejection bother you?

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.948
Do you ever think about it?

00:10:26.948 --> 00:10:29.541
No, it doesn't bother me, I
never think about it much.

00:10:29.541 --> 00:10:31.805
But let me just correct that.

00:10:31.805 --> 00:10:34.218
It does bother you.

00:10:34.218 --> 00:10:37.609
Until a person recognizes
the presence of rejection

00:10:37.609 --> 00:10:41.513
in their life, and
discovers the source of it,

00:10:41.513 --> 00:10:45.682
and deals with it, it will
bother you all of your life.

00:10:45.682 --> 00:10:47.849
Let's just think for a moment and clarify

00:10:47.849 --> 00:10:49.480
what we mean by rejection.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.394
And the truth is if somebody rejects

00:10:51.394 --> 00:10:53.686
something that means they refuse it.

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:56.319
If you come to me and say
I'd like to be your friend

00:10:56.319 --> 00:10:58.103
and I reject you, what I'm saying is,

00:10:58.103 --> 00:10:59.590
I don't want to be your friend.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.591
I refuse your offer of friendship.

00:11:02.591 --> 00:11:03.981
And what does that do?

00:11:03.981 --> 00:11:06.965
That causes the other
person to feel less respect

00:11:06.965 --> 00:11:09.682
for themselves, less worthy of themselves,

00:11:09.682 --> 00:11:13.286
and to begin to be self-critical
for the simple reason,

00:11:13.286 --> 00:11:15.933
why wouldn't somebody
want to be my friend?

00:11:15.933 --> 00:11:18.134
And so, there's some basic things

00:11:18.134 --> 00:11:20.885
that are very basic when it comes to that,

00:11:20.885 --> 00:11:23.364
and what it does, it sends a message.

00:11:23.364 --> 00:11:25.799
In other words, rejection
isn't just a feeling,

00:11:25.799 --> 00:11:27.204
it sends a message.

00:11:27.204 --> 00:11:29.616
When you reject somebody you send them

00:11:29.616 --> 00:11:32.993
a strong message going straight
to the core of their heart,

00:11:32.993 --> 00:11:35.543
you're not worthy, you're not fit,

00:11:35.543 --> 00:11:37.991
you don't belong, I don't want you.

00:11:37.991 --> 00:11:40.715
You don't fit into this situation.

00:11:40.715 --> 00:11:42.914
And anytime any body feels that,

00:11:42.914 --> 00:11:46.003
especially from somebody
that's very precious to them,

00:11:46.003 --> 00:11:48.747
or very important to
them, it's devastating.

00:11:48.747 --> 00:11:51.282
If you don't feel rejected,
if you're not careful,

00:11:51.282 --> 00:11:53.097
you'll reject somebody else.

00:11:53.097 --> 00:11:56.162
But more than likely, all of
us at some point have been.

00:11:56.162 --> 00:11:58.187
And what I want to show you is this,

00:11:58.187 --> 00:12:00.746
just because you think
you have forgotten it,

00:12:00.746 --> 00:12:03.603
doesn't mean that you don't still have it.

00:12:03.603 --> 00:12:05.883
The question is what do you do with it,

00:12:05.883 --> 00:12:07.280
how do you handle it?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.723
And there are lots of ways
people handle rejection

00:12:09.723 --> 00:12:11.243
that doesn't free them of it.

00:12:11.243 --> 00:12:13.682
What I want to talk about
is how you get free of it.

00:12:13.682 --> 00:12:18.348
There is a way to overcome
that, no matter what it is.

00:12:18.348 --> 00:12:22.430
There are three feelings
that are absolutely essential

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:25.597
to a healthy self-attitude and a self,

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:29.871
and your own personal view of yourself.

00:12:29.871 --> 00:12:32.081
Your self-respect and everything else.

00:12:32.081 --> 00:12:34.164
These three attitudes are

00:12:35.855 --> 00:12:38.438
a sense of belonging, I belong.

00:12:39.734 --> 00:12:42.495
That's very important, to
be a part, I'm a part of.

00:12:42.495 --> 00:12:44.912
The second one is I'm worthy.

00:12:47.448 --> 00:12:49.340
That is, you know what?

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:53.542
I'm worth something, I'm
of value, God loves me.

00:12:53.542 --> 00:12:55.792
And thirdly, I'm competent.

00:12:57.777 --> 00:13:00.813
I can do it, I can handle
it, whatever it is.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:04.428
If you don't have those three
feelings about yourself,

00:13:04.428 --> 00:13:06.572
emotions about yourself, you will go

00:13:06.572 --> 00:13:09.138
through life suffering and hurting.

00:13:09.138 --> 00:13:12.771
Healthy body, a healthy
body is always important

00:13:12.771 --> 00:13:14.789
for the simple reason you feel better,

00:13:14.789 --> 00:13:16.876
you're more highly
motivated, you are cheerful,

00:13:16.876 --> 00:13:19.221
you're happy, you're excited and people

00:13:19.221 --> 00:13:21.941
like to be around a person like that.

00:13:21.941 --> 00:13:25.050
And then when I think about
our relationships to others.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.489
Without good relationships to other people

00:13:27.489 --> 00:13:29.304
you're not going to make it in life.

00:13:29.304 --> 00:13:32.503
We're not lone rangers, God's
made us to work and labor

00:13:32.503 --> 00:13:35.254
and fellowship and have
fun with other people.

00:13:35.254 --> 00:13:39.307
Why would a city known for its red economy

00:13:39.307 --> 00:13:42.057
over all these years go bankrupt?

00:13:46.049 --> 00:13:48.299
Why would they go bankrupt?

00:13:49.184 --> 00:13:53.351
Unwise decisions that
probably started years before.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:59.532
Why would a family choose
to buy a home, house,

00:13:59.532 --> 00:14:02.626
that they know that they cannot afford?

00:14:02.626 --> 00:14:05.264
But they're going to buy it anyway.

00:14:05.264 --> 00:14:06.597
Unwise decision.

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:12.477
Why would a person marry just
for a sexual fulfillment?

00:14:13.994 --> 00:14:16.988
Not thinking about other things.

00:14:16.988 --> 00:14:18.321
Unwise decision.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:24.356
Why would a person
drink alcoholic beverage

00:14:24.356 --> 00:14:27.773
in front of their children early in life,

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.217
leaving them an image of their
dad sometimes being drunk,

00:14:34.682 --> 00:14:37.243
thinking nothing of the consequence?

00:14:37.243 --> 00:14:38.993
Very unwise decision.

00:14:40.092 --> 00:14:42.187
When you think about the kind of life

00:14:42.187 --> 00:14:45.067
that you're living would
you say that the decisions

00:14:45.067 --> 00:14:48.541
that you're making are wise or unwise?

00:14:48.541 --> 00:14:50.802
And we could go through
life thinking about

00:14:50.802 --> 00:14:52.474
all the decisions that people make.

00:14:52.474 --> 00:14:56.768
For example, they stack up
credit on their credit cards

00:14:56.768 --> 00:15:00.308
to the point that they know
they can't make the payments.

00:15:00.308 --> 00:15:01.535
Why do they do that?

00:15:01.535 --> 00:15:03.187
Unwise decisions.

00:15:03.187 --> 00:15:04.868
Before you make any decision

00:15:04.868 --> 00:15:07.037
you should always ask this question.

00:15:07.037 --> 00:15:09.620
Is this the wisest thing to do?

00:15:10.949 --> 00:15:13.012
There is always an answer.

00:15:13.012 --> 00:15:15.188
Is this the wisest thing to do?

00:15:15.188 --> 00:15:18.269
Whether it's marriage, or
whether it's something financial,

00:15:18.269 --> 00:15:20.068
or health, or whatever it might be.

00:15:20.068 --> 00:15:22.276
Is this the wisest thing to do?

00:15:22.276 --> 00:15:24.569
That's always the right question

00:15:24.569 --> 00:15:26.682
whether it's major or minor.

00:15:26.682 --> 00:15:29.306
Is this the wisest thing to do?

00:15:29.306 --> 00:15:32.223
But living wisely is the best life.

00:15:33.782 --> 00:15:35.949
Wisdom is a gift from God.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:41.770
Living unwisely is a
very expensive lifestyle

00:15:44.597 --> 00:15:46.994
to every aspect of our life.

00:15:46.994 --> 00:15:51.452
When there's laughter and
there's love and there's joy,

00:15:51.452 --> 00:15:54.889
your body is going to respond accordingly.

00:15:54.889 --> 00:15:58.722
But if you're uptight
and you're not laughing,

00:16:01.107 --> 00:16:03.743
and if you'll just
think about what happens

00:16:03.743 --> 00:16:07.910
to your whole nervous
system when you can't laugh.

00:16:08.945 --> 00:16:10.425
And somebody says well,

00:16:10.425 --> 00:16:12.496
I don't have anything to laugh about.

00:16:12.496 --> 00:16:15.012
Well, yes you do, if you
think about it you do.

00:16:15.012 --> 00:16:17.394
There are times when we
don't feel like laughing.

00:16:17.394 --> 00:16:19.593
If you can't laugh, I'm not too sure

00:16:19.593 --> 00:16:21.139
you've got many friends.

00:16:21.139 --> 00:16:22.126
(congregation laughing)

00:16:22.126 --> 00:16:25.032
Who wants to be around
a grouch all the time?

00:16:25.032 --> 00:16:27.890
Always frowning, there's
always something wrong.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.707
And when you say, well let me tell you

00:16:29.707 --> 00:16:32.111
something good happened
to me; I'm not interested.

00:16:32.111 --> 00:16:34.752
Well when people have that
attitude I believe your

00:16:34.752 --> 00:16:38.313
nervous system is affected,
your whole system is affected.

00:16:38.313 --> 00:16:42.510
I think there's some simple
things God placed in our life

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:47.456
and in the process of exercising
them, we'll live longer.

00:16:47.456 --> 00:16:49.447
Now you say, "Can you prove that?"

00:16:49.447 --> 00:16:52.047
Well, so far I can. (laughs)

00:16:52.047 --> 00:16:54.308
(congregation laughing)

00:16:54.308 --> 00:16:56.137
So far I can.

00:16:56.137 --> 00:16:58.700
(congregation clapping)

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:02.296
And one of the things I
love about my friends is

00:17:02.296 --> 00:17:05.306
we're always jabbing each
other and one of my friends,

00:17:05.306 --> 00:17:07.525
I think all of them are
sitting here this morning.

00:17:07.525 --> 00:17:10.438
Not all my friends, but we're
always jabbing each other

00:17:10.438 --> 00:17:12.749
about something, we're always laughing.

00:17:12.749 --> 00:17:16.469
And I think that frees
up your nervous system.

00:17:16.469 --> 00:17:19.105
Something happens when you're laughing.

00:17:19.105 --> 00:17:22.222
So if you're going to be useful
all the days of your life

00:17:22.222 --> 00:17:26.807
you not only have to be learning
and loving, but laughing.

00:17:26.807 --> 00:17:29.751
So you may say, well, I don't
have anything to laugh about.

00:17:29.751 --> 00:17:31.082
Well, make something.

00:17:31.082 --> 00:17:31.915
(congregation laughing)

00:17:31.915 --> 00:17:33.133
Get something going.

00:17:33.133 --> 00:17:36.883
And watch something that
will help you laugh.

00:17:39.807 --> 00:17:41.659
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:41.659 --> 00:17:44.028
I made this video because
Inga Bowman asked me to.

00:17:44.028 --> 00:17:46.030
If there's someone
you'd like me to profile

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:47.789
in the next Top 10, check out the link

00:17:47.789 --> 00:17:50.302
in the description and
go and cast your vote.

00:17:50.302 --> 00:17:51.913
I'd also love to know what was

00:17:51.913 --> 00:17:53.721
your favorite message from this video?

00:17:53.721 --> 00:17:55.190
What did you learn from this video

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:57.541
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:17:57.541 --> 00:17:59.073
in your life or in your business?

00:17:59.073 --> 00:18:00.809
Please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:18:00.809 --> 00:18:02.072
I'm really curious to find out.

00:18:02.072 --> 00:18:04.482
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Kelly Quittenton.

00:18:04.482 --> 00:18:07.098
Kelly thank you so much for
picking up 10 copies of my book,

00:18:07.098 --> 00:18:09.799
Your One Word, and sending
them out to your friends.

00:18:09.799 --> 00:18:12.289
I hope you and they really enjoy the read.

00:18:12.289 --> 00:18:14.849
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:18:14.849 --> 00:18:16.925
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:18:16.925 --> 00:18:19.144
and whatever your one word is.

00:18:19.144 --> 00:18:22.120
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:25.203
(whooshing and boom)

00:18:28.189 --> 00:18:29.906
- Kelly, how are you?

00:18:29.906 --> 00:18:31.618
I'm meeting your dad here

00:18:31.618 --> 00:18:34.397
and he's very excited about you.

00:18:34.397 --> 00:18:36.249
And he just wanted me to say hi to you

00:18:36.249 --> 00:18:37.649
so I just want to say hi.

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:39.537
I hope the Lord will bless you good,

00:18:39.537 --> 00:18:42.727
and hopefully one day you
can come with him, thanks.

